From: OpenWrt aic8800 packaging
Subject: [PATCH] SDIO: rx: tell FORTIFY the radiotap area is rtap_len bytes

The 6.12 kernel builds this driver with FORTIFY_SOURCE, which rejects the
HE radiotap write:

    fortify-string.h:571:25: error: call to '__write_overflow_field'
      declared with attribute warning: detected write beyond size of
      field (1st parameter); maybe use struct_group()?

It is a provenance problem, not an overflow. rwnx_rx_rtap_hdrlen() adds
ALIGN(len, 2) + sizeof(struct ieee80211_radiotap_he) under exactly the
condition and alignment this writer uses, and the buffer comes from
skb_push(skb, rtap_len) - but the compiler only sees pos derived from a
pointer to the 8-byte radiotap header.

Use unsafe_memcpy() at this one call site with that reasoning recorded,
rather than demoting -Wattribute-warning for the whole driver, so a
genuine fortify hit anywhere else still stops the build.
---
--- a/src/SDIO/driver_fw/driver/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_rx.c
+++ b/src/SDIO/driver_fw/driver/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_rx.c
@@ -1437,7 +1437,22 @@
 		while ((pos - (u8 *)rtap) & 1)
 			pos++;
 		rtap->it_present |= cpu_to_le32(1 << IEEE80211_RADIOTAP_HE);
+		/*
+		 * FORTIFY_SOURCE traces pos back to rtap, whose type is just the
+		 * 8-byte radiotap header, and so reads this as a write past the
+		 * end of a field. The buffer is really rtap_len bytes - see the
+		 * skb_push() at the top of this function - and
+		 * rwnx_rx_rtap_hdrlen() reserves ALIGN(len, 2) plus sizeof(struct
+		 * ieee80211_radiotap_he) under the same HE_SU condition and the
+		 * same alignment this writer uses. The write is in bounds; only
+		 * its provenance is unprovable to the compiler.
+		 */
+#ifdef unsafe_memcpy
+		unsafe_memcpy(pos, &he, sizeof(he),
+			      /* radiotap area is rtap_len bytes, see rwnx_rx_rtap_hdrlen() */);
+#else
 		memcpy(pos, &he, sizeof(he));
+#endif
 		pos += sizeof(he);
 	}
 
